s at a time,[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]until no workable task bead remains.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]2[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202610/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]backlog_epic_2_top_five_task_beads.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202610/backlog_epic_2_top_five_task_beads.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-1ou[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-1ou/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Make the flake-baseline gate reach a truthful verdict again [/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF](sase-1og)[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]flake-baseline[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]flake-baseline: drop the duplicate fixed-at directive that makes [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tools/selection_health --fail-on-new-flake exit 2, add a regression test[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]that parses the committed baseline, then reconcile the 64 exceedances [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the unmasked gate reports (fixed-at for verified fixes, baseline entries[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]only under existing open beads, follow-ups for the rest), and close [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase-1og.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Stop the ToolRun store failing with \"database is locked\" under[bold white on #D75F87][/bold #D7AFFF] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]parallel load (sase-18t)[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]toolrun-busy[dim] · [dim][/dim]after flake-baseline[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]toolrun-busy: identify which sase-core ToolRun store transactions hold [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the SQLite write lock while launcher, settle and show paths read it, fix[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the contention at its source in sase-core with a principled busy policy,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]move the core pin, retire the tests/tool/ baseline entries with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]fixed-at, and close sase-18t.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Make the weight-two land-agent-session capacity e2e [/bold #D7AFFF]          [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]load-robust (sase-12f)[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]capacity-e2e[dim] · [dim][/dim]after flake-baseline[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]capacity-e2e: find what consumes the fakey land agent's 5 s budget under[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]load in tests/fakey/test_monitor_capacity_e2e.py (delayed child [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bootstrap, capacity scan under the host-wide slot lock, or harness [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]polling), fix the cause instead of the timeout, prove it with a loaded [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]stress loop, and close sase-12f.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Fix the Files ctrl+j page-anchor scroll race (sase-1a7)[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]deck-anchor[dim] · [dim][/dim]after flake-baseline[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]deck-anchor: reproduce the intermittent wait_for_anchor_scroll timeout [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]in test_files_ctrl_j_scrolls_page_anchor_to_top (it fails about 1 in 4 [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]even in isolation), fix the Files spread scroll/anchor race in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]production code, prove it with isolated and loaded stress loops, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]close sase-1a7.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Rotate and purge the historical secret-scanner hits in public [bold white on #D75F87][/bold #D7AFFF] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]sase--agents history (sase-1ot)[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]agents-secret-purge[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]agents-secret-purge: triage the 27 private-audit findings without [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]printing values, hand the owner a rotation checklist, design and gate a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]reviewed history purge of sase-org/sase--agents that quiesces [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]publication and resets every clone, re-audit the purged tip, and close [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase-1ot.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-1ou","llm_provider":"muse","model":"muse-spark-1.3-contributor","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-1ou.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-e54e8e716d493f67dad944a0e291d609","started_at":"2026-10-27T13:23:39.728001+00:00","state":"completed"},{"capabilities":{"durably_revivable":true,"historically_viewable":true,"missing_requirements":[],"restartable":true},"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"chat":{"digest":"b3b32b348203148f72c2f342081331d136738b7d602ddc7e202774fdf23ec13d","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-1ou.5.1.3--plan/chat.md","size_bytes":4952},"commits":{"digest":"8e7b7391dee0fbc777c8f04760044a8b219226315cfa053ba293f842ac7f99e9","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-1ou.5.1.3--plan/commits.json","size_bytes":89},"embedded_workflows":{"digest":"a398c70160fe308637edd70b38d8cf02cc697183c480675d10f387d529663058","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-1ou.5.1.3--plan/embedded_workflows.json","size_bytes":80},"meta":{"digest":"3d52e403878458500021d2379e830e92e386f03f3507cd392b339032948f2749","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-1ou.5.1.3--plan/meta.json","size_bytes":831},"prompt":{"digest":"7d2a9b10113bd6d4993e487798f68080a252b2846988465a0bb5fb411ba51805","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-1ou.5.1.3--plan/prompt.md","size_bytes":222},"prompt_steps":{"digest":"0424d0c195e1b23f4639d8f7731f8d93db484a21eafb1b5d825e9f42baf79062","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-1ou.5.1.3--plan/prompt_steps.json","size_bytes":8361},"state":{"d